module

public import Mathlib.Algebra.Lie.AdjointAction.Derivation
public import TauCeti.Algebra.Lie.Derivation.TaylorExp
public import TauCeti.Algebra.Lie.Presentation.Serre.Integrable

/-!
# The simple reflections of a Serre system permute its weight spaces

Let `(H, E, F)` be a Serre system for a matrix of integers `CM` in a Lie algebra `L`
(`TauCeti.IsSerreSystem`), and suppose that the raising and lowering families `E` and `F` generate
`L`. The motivating example is the Lie algebra `Matrix.ToLieAlgebra K CM` presented by Serre's
relations, with its own generators. By `TauCeti/Algebra/Lie/Presentation/Serre/Integrable.lean`,
`ad Eᵢ` and `ad Fᵢ` act locally nilpotently on `L`, so when the additive group of `L` is a
`ℚ`-module their Taylor exponentials (`LieDerivation.taylorExp`) are automorphisms of `L`, and so is

`θᵢ = exp (ad Eᵢ) ∘ exp (ad (-Fᵢ)) ∘ exp (ad Eᵢ)`

(`TauCeti.IsSerreSystem.weylAut`). These are Kac's automorphisms (written `rᵢ` with a
tilde), the Lie-algebra shadows of the group elements `x_{αᵢ}(1) x_{-αᵢ}(-1) x_{αᵢ}(1)`
representing the simple reflections. The construction has the same shape as the Weyl automorphism
`TauCeti.weylAut` of an `sl₂` triple: if moreover `CMᵢᵢ = 2` and `Hᵢ ≠ 0`, so that `(Hᵢ, Eᵢ, Fᵢ)` is
an `sl₂` triple, and `ad Eᵢ` and `ad Fᵢ` are nilpotent, then the three Taylor exponentials are
Mathlib's exponentials (`LieDerivation.taylorExp_eq_exp`), which are the ones `TauCeti.weylAut`
composes. No comparison lemma between the two automorphisms is stated here. Only the local
nilpotence of `ad Eᵢ` and `ad Fᵢ` is used, and no global nilpotence bound is assumed.

When `CMᵢᵢ = 2`, the automorphism `θᵢ` acts on the Cartan generators by the simple coreflection

`θᵢ (Hₖ) = Hₖ - CMₖᵢ • Hᵢ`

(`TauCeti.IsSerreSystem.weylAut_apply_H`), and so does its inverse. Write `L_χ` for the
simultaneous eigenspace `⨅ k, (ad Hₖ).eigenspace χₖ` of an integral weight `χ : B → ℤ`, and
`sᵢ χ = χ - χᵢ • CM.col i` for its reflection in the weight `CM.col i` of `Eᵢ`. Transporting the
eigenvalue equations along `θᵢ` gives

`θᵢ (L_χ) = L_{sᵢ χ}`

(`TauCeti.IsSerreSystem.map_weylAut_iInf_eigenspace`). So the weight spaces `L_χ` and
`L_{sᵢ χ}` are isomorphic, and the set of weights of `L` is stable under the simple reflections
`sᵢ`. This is the Weyl-group symmetry of the weight spaces used in Serre's theorem. Under the
additional hypotheses of that theorem (a Cartan matrix of finite type, whose roots are all real),
it reduces the study of the weight spaces at roots and their multiples to those at simple roots
and their multiples, which are treated, under their own hypotheses, by
`TauCeti.IsSerreSystem.iInf_eigenspace_ad_col_eq_span_singleton` and
`TauCeti.IsSerreSystem.iInf_eigenspace_ad_nsmul_col_eq_bot`.

## Main definitions

* `TauCeti.IsSerreSystem.weylAut`: the automorphism `exp (ad Eᵢ) ∘ exp (ad (-Fᵢ)) ∘ exp (ad Eᵢ)`
  of a Lie algebra generated by a Serre system.

## Main results

* `TauCeti.IsSerreSystem.weylAut_apply_H` and `TauCeti.IsSerreSystem.weylAut_symm_apply_H`:
  the automorphism and its inverse act on the `Hₖ` by the simple coreflection.
* `TauCeti.IsSerreSystem.weylAut_mem_iInf_eigenspace`: the automorphism carries `L_χ` into
  `L_{sᵢ χ}`.
* `TauCeti.IsSerreSystem.map_weylAut_iInf_eigenspace`: it carries `L_χ` onto `L_{sᵢ χ}`.
* `TauCeti.IsSerreSystem.exists_lieEquiv_map_iInf_eigenspace` and
  `TauCeti.exists_lieEquiv_map_iInf_eigenspace_serreH`: over a field of characteristic zero, every
  simple reflection of weights is realised by an automorphism of a Lie algebra generated by a Serre
  system, in particular of the Lie algebra presented by Serre's relations.

## References

* [J.P. Serre, *Complex Semisimple Lie Algebras*][serre1965], chapter VI, appendix
* [J. E. Humphreys, *Introduction to Lie Algebras and Representation Theory*][humphreys1972],
  §18.3
* V. G. Kac, *Infinite Dimensional Lie Algebras*, 3rd ed., Cambridge University Press (1990),
  §3.8.
-/

public section

open LieAlgebra

namespace TauCeti

variable {B R L : Type*} [CommRing R] [LieRing L] [LieAlgebra R L] {CM : Matrix B B ℤ}
  {H E F : B → L}

namespace IsSerreSystem

section Reflection

variable [Module ℚ L] (h : IsSerreSystem R CM H E F)
  (hspan : LieSubalgebra.lieSpan R L (Set.range E ∪ Set.range F) = ⊤)

/-! ## The exponentials of the generators -/

omit [Module ℚ L] in
include h hspan in
/-- `ad Eᵢ` is locally nilpotent, in the form required by `LieDerivation.taylorExp`. -/
theorem exists_iterate_ad_E_eq_zero (i : B) (y : L) :
    ∃ n, (LieDerivation.ad R L (E i))^[n] y = 0 := by
  obtain ⟨n, hn⟩ := (LieSubalgebra.mem_engel_iff R (E i) y).1
    (h.engel_E_eq_top hspan i ▸ LieSubalgebra.mem_top y)
  have hc : ⇑(LieDerivation.ad R L (E i)) = ⇑(ad R L (E i)) := funext fun z => by simp
  exact ⟨n, by rw [hc, ← pow_apply_eq_iterate, hn]⟩

omit [Module ℚ L] in
include h hspan in
/-- `ad (-Fᵢ)` is locally nilpotent, in the form required by `LieDerivation.taylorExp`. -/
theorem exists_iterate_ad_neg_F_eq_zero (i : B) (y : L) :
    ∃ n, (LieDerivation.ad R L (-F i))^[n] y = 0 := by
  have hF : LieSubalgebra.engel R (-F i) = ⊤ := by
    rw [LieSubalgebra.engel_neg, h.engel_F_eq_top hspan i]
  obtain ⟨n, hn⟩ := (LieSubalgebra.mem_engel_iff R (-F i) y).1 (hF ▸ LieSubalgebra.mem_top y)
  have hc : ⇑(LieDerivation.ad R L (-F i)) = ⇑(ad R L (-F i)) := funext fun z => by simp
  exact ⟨n, by rw [hc, ← pow_apply_eq_iterate, hn]⟩

/-- The **Weyl automorphism** `exp (ad Eᵢ) ∘ exp (ad (-Fᵢ)) ∘ exp (ad Eᵢ)` of a Lie algebra
generated by a Serre system, Kac's automorphism (written `rᵢ` with a tilde) realising the simple
reflection of weights. The exponentials are Taylor exponentials of the locally nilpotent
derivations `ad Eᵢ` and `ad (-Fᵢ)`; the Serre system and the generation hypothesis are what make
them locally nilpotent. -/
noncomputable def weylAut (i : B) : L ≃ₗ⁅R⁆ L :=
  (LieDerivation.taylorExp _ (h.exists_iterate_ad_E_eq_zero hspan i)).trans
    ((LieDerivation.taylorExp _ (h.exists_iterate_ad_neg_F_eq_zero hspan i)).trans
      (LieDerivation.taylorExp _ (h.exists_iterate_ad_E_eq_zero hspan i)))

/-- The Weyl automorphism as the threefold composite it is defined to be. -/
theorem weylAut_apply (i : B) (x : L) :
    h.weylAut hspan i x =
      LieDerivation.taylorExp _ (h.exists_iterate_ad_E_eq_zero hspan i)
        (LieDerivation.taylorExp _ (h.exists_iterate_ad_neg_F_eq_zero hspan i)
          (LieDerivation.taylorExp _ (h.exists_iterate_ad_E_eq_zero hspan i) x)) :=
  (rfl)

/-! ### The exponentials on the generators -/

section Generators

variable (i : B)

/-- `exp (ad Eᵢ)` sends `Hₖ` to `Hₖ - CMₖᵢ • Eᵢ`. -/
private theorem expE_apply_H (k : B) :
    LieDerivation.taylorExp _ (h.exists_iterate_ad_E_eq_zero hspan i) (H k) =
      H k - CM k i • E i := by
  have h₁ : ⁅E i, H k⁆ = -(CM k i • E i) := by rw [← lie_skew, h.lie_H_E k i]
  rw [LieDerivation.taylorExp_apply_of_apply_apply_eq_zero _ _
    (by simp only [LieDerivation.ad_apply_apply, h₁, lie_neg, lie_zsmul, lie_self, smul_zero,
      neg_zero]),
    LieDerivation.ad_apply_apply, h₁, sub_eq_add_neg]

/-- `exp (ad Eᵢ)` fixes `Eᵢ`. -/
private theorem expE_apply_E :
    LieDerivation.taylorExp _ (h.exists_iterate_ad_E_eq_zero hspan i) (E i) = E i :=
  LieDerivation.taylorExp_apply_of_apply_eq_zero _ _ (by simp)

/-- `exp (ad (-Fᵢ))` sends `Hₖ` to `Hₖ - CMₖᵢ • Fᵢ`. -/
private theorem expF_apply_H (k : B) :
    LieDerivation.taylorExp _ (h.exists_iterate_ad_neg_F_eq_zero hspan i) (H k) =
      H k - CM k i • F i := by
  have h₁ : ⁅-F i, H k⁆ = -(CM k i • F i) := by rw [neg_lie, lie_skew, h.lie_H_F k i]
  rw [LieDerivation.taylorExp_apply_of_apply_apply_eq_zero _ _
    (by simp only [LieDerivation.ad_apply_apply, h₁, lie_neg, lie_zsmul, neg_lie, lie_self,
      smul_zero, neg_zero]),
    LieDerivation.ad_apply_apply, h₁, sub_eq_add_neg]

/-- `exp (ad (-Fᵢ))` sends `Eᵢ` to `Eᵢ + Hᵢ - Fᵢ` when `CMᵢᵢ = 2`. -/
private theorem expF_apply_E (hii : CM i i = 2) :
    LieDerivation.taylorExp _ (h.exists_iterate_ad_neg_F_eq_zero hspan i) (E i) =
      E i + H i - F i := by
  have h₁ : ⁅-F i, E i⁆ = H i := by rw [neg_lie, lie_skew, h.lie_E_F_self i]
  have h₂ : ⁅-F i, H i⁆ = -((2 : ℤ) • F i) := by
    rw [neg_lie, lie_skew, h.lie_H_F i i, hii]
  rw [LieDerivation.taylorExp_apply_of_apply_apply_apply_eq_zero _ _
    (by simp only [LieDerivation.ad_apply_apply, h₁, h₂, lie_neg, lie_zsmul, neg_lie, lie_self,
      smul_zero, neg_zero]),
    LieDerivation.ad_apply_apply, LieDerivation.ad_apply_apply, h₁, h₂, smul_neg,
    ← Int.cast_smul_eq_zsmul ℚ, smul_smul]
  norm_num
  abel

/-- **The Weyl automorphism acts on the Cartan generators by the simple coreflection**:
`θᵢ (Hₖ) = Hₖ - CMₖᵢ • Hᵢ` when `CMᵢᵢ = 2`. -/
@[simp]
theorem weylAut_apply_H (hii : CM i i = 2) (k : B) :
    h.weylAut hspan i (H k) = H k - CM k i • H i := by
  rw [weylAut_apply, h.expE_apply_H hspan i k, map_sub, map_zsmul, h.expF_apply_H hspan i k,
    h.expF_apply_E hspan i hii]
  simp only [map_sub, map_add, map_zsmul, h.expE_apply_H hspan i, h.expE_apply_E hspan i, hii]
  module

/-- The inverse of the Weyl automorphism also acts on the Cartan generators by the simple
coreflection, which is an involution when `CMᵢᵢ = 2`. -/
@[simp]
theorem weylAut_symm_apply_H (hii : CM i i = 2) (k : B) :
    (h.weylAut hspan i).symm (H k) = H k - CM k i • H i := by
  rw [LieEquiv.symm_apply_eq, map_sub, map_zsmul, h.weylAut_apply_H hspan i hii,
    h.weylAut_apply_H hspan i hii, hii]
  module

end Generators

/-! ### The Weyl automorphisms on the weight spaces -/

variable {i : B}

/-- **The Weyl automorphism carries weight vectors to weight vectors**: when `CMᵢᵢ = 2`, it maps
the weight space `L_χ` into the weight space of the reflected weight `χ - χᵢ • CM.col i`. -/
theorem weylAut_mem_iInf_eigenspace (hii : CM i i = 2) {χ : B → ℤ} {x : L}
    (hx : x ∈ ⨅ k, (ad R L (H k)).eigenspace (χ k : R)) :
    h.weylAut hspan i x ∈ ⨅ k, (ad R L (H k)).eigenspace ((χ - χ i • CM.col i) k : R) :=
  (h.weylAut hspan i).apply_mem_iInf_eigenspace_of_symm_apply
    (h.weylAut_symm_apply_H hspan i hii) hx

/-- **The Weyl automorphism permutes the weight spaces**: when `CMᵢᵢ = 2`, it carries the weight
space `L_χ` onto the weight space of the reflected weight `χ - χᵢ • CM.col i`. -/
theorem map_weylAut_iInf_eigenspace (hii : CM i i = 2) (χ : B → ℤ) :
    (⨅ k, (ad R L (H k)).eigenspace (χ k : R)).map
        ((h.weylAut hspan i).toLinearEquiv : L →ₗ[R] L) =
      ⨅ k, (ad R L (H k)).eigenspace ((χ - χ i • CM.col i) k : R) := by
  refine le_antisymm ?_ fun y hy => ?_
  · rintro _ ⟨x, hx, rfl⟩
    exact h.weylAut_mem_iInf_eigenspace hspan hii hx
  · -- the reflection of weights is an involution, and the inverse automorphism reflects back
    have hs : (χ - χ i • CM.col i) - (χ - χ i • CM.col i) i • CM.col i = χ := by
      funext k
      simp only [Pi.sub_apply, Pi.smul_apply, Matrix.col_apply, smul_eq_mul, hii]
      ring
    have hy' := (h.weylAut hspan i).symm.apply_mem_iInf_eigenspace_of_symm_apply
      (fun k => by rw [LieEquiv.symm_symm, h.weylAut_apply_H hspan i hii]) hy
    rw [hs] at hy'
    exact ⟨_, hy', by simp⟩

end Reflection

/-- **Every simple reflection of weights is realised by an automorphism.** In a Lie algebra over a
field of characteristic zero generated by a Serre system with `CMᵢᵢ = 2`, there is an automorphism
acting on the `Hₖ` by the simple coreflection and carrying each weight space `L_χ` onto the weight
space of `χ - χᵢ • CM.col i`. It is the Weyl automorphism `TauCeti.IsSerreSystem.weylAut`, for
the `ℚ`-module structure obtained by restricting scalars. -/
theorem exists_lieEquiv_map_iInf_eigenspace {K : Type*} [Field K] [CharZero K] [LieAlgebra K L]
    (h : IsSerreSystem K CM H E F)
    (hspan : LieSubalgebra.lieSpan K L (Set.range E ∪ Set.range F) = ⊤) {i : B}
    (hii : CM i i = 2) :
    ∃ τ : L ≃ₗ⁅K⁆ L, (∀ k, τ (H k) = H k - CM k i • H i) ∧ ∀ χ : B → ℤ,
      (⨅ k, (ad K L (H k)).eigenspace (χ k : K)).map (τ.toLinearEquiv : L →ₗ[K] L) =
        ⨅ k, (ad K L (H k)).eigenspace ((χ - χ i • CM.col i) k : K) := by
  let _ : Module ℚ L := Module.compHom L (algebraMap ℚ K)
  exact ⟨h.weylAut hspan i, h.weylAut_apply_H hspan i hii,
    h.map_weylAut_iInf_eigenspace hspan hii⟩

end IsSerreSystem

/-- **The simple reflections of the presented algebra.** Over a field of characteristic zero, for
every index `i` with `CMᵢᵢ = 2` the Lie algebra presented by Serre's relations has an automorphism
acting on the generators `Hₖ` by the simple coreflection and carrying each weight space `L_χ` onto
the weight space of `χ - χᵢ • CM.col i`. -/
theorem exists_lieEquiv_map_iInf_eigenspace_serreH [DecidableEq B] (CM : Matrix B B ℤ)
    (K : Type*) [Field K] [CharZero K] {i : B} (hii : CM i i = 2) :
    ∃ τ : Matrix.ToLieAlgebra K CM ≃ₗ⁅K⁆ Matrix.ToLieAlgebra K CM,
      (∀ k, τ (serreH K CM k) = serreH K CM k - CM k i • serreH K CM i) ∧ ∀ χ : B → ℤ,
        (⨅ k, (ad K _ (serreH K CM k)).eigenspace (χ k : K)).map
            (τ.toLinearEquiv : Matrix.ToLieAlgebra K CM →ₗ[K] Matrix.ToLieAlgebra K CM) =
          ⨅ k, (ad K _ (serreH K CM k)).eigenspace ((χ - χ i • CM.col i) k : K) :=
  (isSerreSystem_serre K CM).exists_lieEquiv_map_iInf_eigenspace
    (lieSpan_serreE_union_serreF_eq_top K CM) hii

end TauCeti
